// Local signing configuration. The project intentionally does NOT hardcode a
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM (it used to, before this went open source — a personal
// Apple Developer Team ID has no business being in a public repo). The
// simplest fix, and what most people should do: open the project in Xcode,
// select the BoosteroidATV target → Signing & Capabilities, and pick your own
// team there (Automatic signing). Xcode writes that choice to your local
// project state, not to project.pbxproj, so it never gets committed.
//
// If you'd rather manage it via an xcconfig instead (e.g. for CI, or to keep
// it out of Xcode's UI-managed state entirely): copy this file to
// Local.xcconfig, fill in your Team ID below, then in Xcode go to the
// project (not target) → Info tab → set each configuration's "Based on" to
// Local.xcconfig. Local.xcconfig itself is git-ignored, so it stays yours.
// Find your Team ID at developer.apple.com → Account → Membership.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID_HERE
